Version 1.2 (19 August 2026):
=============================

* gsummary.data.frame():
- new argument: "digits"
- new column in the returned print whenever factors are present: "is.factor()"

* gsummary.lm():
- new argument: "digits"
- the returned print contains less scientific notation (p-values in particular)

* gsummary.glm():
- new argument: "digits"
- the returned print contains less scientific notation (p-values in particular)


